[?2004l[?2004h>   "type": "javascript",
[?2004l[?2004h>   "function": "function(){java.lang.Runtime.getRuntime().exec('malicious_command');}",
[?2004l[?2004h>   "": {
[?2004l[?2004h>     "enabled": true
[?2004l[?2004h>   }
[?2004l[?2004h> }
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Fix Description
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> This patch adds validation to the `JavaScriptDimFilter` class to:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Block Dangerous Java API Calls**: The `validateConfiguration()` method checks if the JavaScript function contains calls to dangerous Java APIs that could be used for code execution:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - `java.lang.Runtime`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - `java.lang.ProcessBuilder`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - `java.io.File`
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Early Validation**: The validation is performed in the constructor, ensuring that malicious payloads are rejected immediately upon deserialization.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Files Modified
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - `processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/filter/JavaScriptDimFilter.java`
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Added `validateConfiguration()` method
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Added validation call in the `@JsonCreator` constructor
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Patch Files
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - `0001-fix-javascript-filter-empty-key-vulnerability.patch` - Main security fix
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## How to Apply
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. Navigate to the Druid source directory:
[?2004l[?2004h>    ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>    cd /root/druid
